{
  "_comment": "Five-sleeve engine config (2026-11-07, DRAFT): the armed design as of 2026-11-07 (sleeves S, M, C, O, the BOXX reserve, the 60 % trades cap) plus sleeve T = THE MONTH-END BOND BOOK (scan monthend, lib/two-sleeve/monthend-scan.js): TLT at 10 % of the book, bought at the 15:55 print of the month's third-to-last session and sold at the 15:55 print of its last (the 12:55 print on a 13:00 close), nights and weekends held. Measured: the 10-year yield falls 2-3 bp over that window out of sample since 1990; TLT net of 7.8 bp +0.33 % a hold 2004-2015 and +0.22 % 2016-2026, 21 of 23 years positive; through the engine at 10 %, decade 0.2114 -> 0.2175 %/wk, Sharpe 2.37 -> 2.43, worst week unchanged, no -2 % week, the other sleeves trade-for-trade unchanged; it never crosses the 60 % trades cap at 10 % (ledger rows tier0-month-end-yields-oos-1962-2003, tier1-tlt-month-end-book-13-windows, tier2-tlt-month-end-book-30-quarters, desc-t-overlay-placebo-offsets-2016-2026, desc-t-book-exposure-cash-2026-11). Small: about +0.3 %/yr. T is LAST in order, so the day sleeves and the night book claim first. Its env is O's (entry gates off, exits off, weekends held, no Friday block, the stable knobs pinned off) with T's size (10 %, one slot) and TRADER_MAX_HOLD_SESSIONS=4 as the backstop for a missed sale. TRADER_MONTHEND_SHADOW=1 here = journal-only (monthend_shadow / monthend_shadow_exit rows in T.scan.jsonl); set it to 0 to arm. Arming is the operator's call: copy the T block and the order into the engine's config.json and relaunch outside market hours.",
